{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"The **trust’s board of trustees selects the independent public accountant**, with approval by a majority of trustees who are not “interested persons” under the Investment Company Act—not the adviser or audit committee acting alone. The audit committee typically recommends the firm.\n\nUnder **Section 32(a)(2)**, selection ordinarily goes to the next annual shareholders’ meeting **if one is held**. Ratification can be omitted:\n\n- **If no annual meeting is held**; ETFs generally need not hold annual meetings solely for auditor ratification.\n- **Under Rule 32a-4**, even if an annual meeting occurs, where the fund has an entirely independent audit committee overseeing accounting and auditing, a charter describing its structure, duties, powers and operating methods, and permanently maintains that charter in an easily accessible place.\n\n**Worth knowing:** A multi-series structure does not itself create an exemption; the applicable fund requirements must be satisfied."}}
